    <node id="星核">
      <data key="d0">星核</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Stellaron (星核) is an immensely powerful, mysterious, and highly dangerous alien celestial object that acts as a root cause of widespread disasters across worlds. It functions like a cancer, creating Fragmentum corruption that generates new spaces, alters environments, and blocks space-time, often disrupting the routes of the Astral Express. Its fall brings calamities such as eternal freezes and invasions, and it can connect to Paths or Aeon powers, often responding to a civilization’s desires in the form of catastrophe, potentially linking it to the Destruction Aeon, Nanook. Originally a unique collection piece at the Herta Space Station, a Stellaron was removed and implanted within the body of the Trailblazer by the Stellaron Hunters, granting them power but posing a constant, stabilized threat.

On Jarilo-VI (Belobog), the Stellaron is the central crisis, hidden deep within the world, responsible for the eternal winter, the expansion of the Fragmentum, and the separation of upper and lower cities. After the Supreme Guardian Cocolia’s alliance with it was broken, the eternal freeze began to recede, though the Fragmentum did not completely disappear. On the Xianzhou Luofu, a Stellaron was smuggled past security and planted at the base of the Ambrosial Arbor, making it the culprit behind the Arbor’s rebirth, exploited by Phantylia and groups like the药王秘传 to incite self-destruction.

In Penacony, the Stellaron is a critical narrative element and the core of the dream. It is located within the Penacony Grand Theater, serving as a part of the absolute stage for the Harmony Grand Ceremony. The Family controls it, and it is the root cause of the ceremony’s suspension. The Watchmaker confirms its existence, and it is a dangerous force manipulated by someone, with the Dreammaster denying responsibility. It is an objective the characters prioritize, as sealing it is essential to save Penacony, whose dream is built upon it. Additionally, a "Stellaron disaster" changed the planet Lushaka, and the Stellaron was used by the "Order" to catalyze the merging of Asdana's Mnemonic Matter with the material world.</data>
