    <node id="瓦尔特">
      <data key="d0">瓦尔特</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Welt Yang, also known as "Uncle Yang" or "Mr. Yang," is a mature, experienced, and rational senior member of the Astral Express Crew who upholds the Trailblaze philosophy. He joined the crew after being rescued and works to pay off his rescue costs. Prior to joining the Express, Welt worked as an animator but left his home world to fight against extraterrestrial invaders called the "Sky People," retaining a personal wish to return home. On the team, he provides philosophical perspectives, tactical analysis, and guidance, often checking the Trailblazer's heroic traits and explaining phenomena like warp travel and the Fragmentum. Welt is thoughtful and strategic, preferring diplomacy over conflict. He has worked with Himeko to suppress a Stellaron and clarifies their mission to seal it.

During the Penacony visit, Welt comments on its complexities and the "Watchmaker," analyzes the words of Sparkle and The Family, and believes a third party is involved. He investigates the dreamscape settlement, analyzes dreams as thought traps, discusses the influence of "Harmony" in Penacony, and suspects external forces affecting the family's ideology. He engages in philosophical dialogue with Acheron, sharing a story of a man from his homeland who created a "spiritual Adam." He directly questioned the Dreammaster and posed a critical question at the ritual's end about whether the god worshipped by The Family was actually Xipe. He was imprisoned in his consciousness by Sunday's "Tuning" ability and learned the history of the Order Aeon, but was rescued after the defeat of the Choir. He also observed a dissonant sound within the music of Order, representing people awakening for freedom in Penacony. As a member of the Express, he participates in negotiations and logically analyzes situations to vote for destinations, supporting going to Edostar and commenting on the Trailblazer's growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99d6c8ac9917f5a8ab265464fbd40c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bf92db6fb06a4ce23bb9a1040ac0bf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a4d47602d8436e5950b7c64fa6734&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789285bc757b7b48d94a58fb5071cb0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010cf81a86ef8e6d81978812db1537ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95f3cdca78469e141c72057fa03532b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91f7fcf2745a1b4cb918633cb92877ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0e0a01514bf55bdf01a37e57b42711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb530c0e05d34c67f0c09a0b64e8fa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575eb06637f7ecf24d773fb6f0f798b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0bd49528edf3e917eef4f2c1aa6516&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52f0fb910ea43e4acb7d09e5d8281a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f363a6ba12d7e65941adba654ef6fb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2decb49a546c2b4fde6ed99f9c7b7ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9509992da819b3c05c5d00771b2ec521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c308352492cacde7b8e6f6802f949905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f371fb32e3b3a665db31402cdb619141&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33140787e65f36d03a2cf1fe766a0e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992f8ca9cbe3142dda05033f0b52e1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076f9df9869a74ed98d14ab2d4cf67a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e80256f6b29768c5cfabe6c8af4d081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63dc2a8cef74048f287c7e0648930116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1ac3b2477b33ac600764c2339c9761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94c423af9b3a1e7696ea7c8396c60833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08335684ed867f94f55ddc89bffdc37f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-807438542660c564cc6c45c1235307a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bbc2acab19c28d156b60535056e250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7304e1604bff47c393b7d5c5dec23a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a08a4c1f5ae941cbe079fc5aaa48a0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef607cf0570a332c394810669c8b2ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079eb38c9a9466ff33a065e348bc39a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d49ee9d93d2b9c97270455c78b3b83e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6bc51c0b8f913f809328ba29170426&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29856bd40ae5205b29c5ab0965af404a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7823732295dacca3169a4fdc0d9b7a6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43623aa0b2e27c60a1de27a0205f0f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbab5d9a926ed72d8916642b162a156f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecd9bc285c1eb0c1092ea17d790b9a54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-488e16522a18a4f6bb0a292766e58c72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6e390686a60c1282db4fe45d6c892f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c824b5ac58cbd