    <node id="长生种">
      <data key="d0">长生种</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The concept of 长生种 (Long-Lived Species) refers to beings with extremely long lifespans, most notably the inhabitants of the Xianzhou Alliance who gained their longevity after consuming the fruit of the Arbor. These individuals possess nearly infinite lifespans but suffer from inherent biological and psychological drawbacks: their memory capacity is limited, and as the centuries pass, their emotional thresholds rise due to accumulated wear and tear. Over time, this can ultimately lead to the condition known as 魔阴身 (Mara-Struck). Due to their extended lives, long-lived species tend to recall distant events as recent history and are generally less accustomed to elaborate funeral rites. They also have unique capacities for enduring suffering and pain over prolonged periods. Despite their immortality, the Xianzhou people are still considered a long-lived species rather than truly immortal, as they are still subject to 魔阴身.&lt;SEP&gt;长生种are long-lived species in the Xianzhou, including the Xianzhou natives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a9abe8221b156371ccb92c8c70ff3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e44ecf966c6560c7f086afff655868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b1f262b5a3808ba99b93f0ef466c358&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0f25ff767eb93fbf9b6c961acfd724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47555a254b36325300969067b357d5ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fc6126d0155a7c411f4068a66d7ddca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc2240f2b9c03c7ee20a149da420ca0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-024d2e72f6f7b12c92caa76b22df8be2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1778833963</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="狐人">
      <data key="d0">狐人</data>
      <data key="d1">faction</data>
      <data key="d2">The Foxian people are a faction and species within the Xianzhou Alliance. As a long-life species, they are less susceptible to Marasylum due to their limited lifespan compared to other long-life races, though they are still considered a short-lived race on the Xianzhou. Foxians serve in various roles within the Alliance, including in the天舶司 (Sky-Faring Commission). They have unique cultural and funeral customs, such as launching starskiffs carrying their deceased into the stars, and specific traditions involving kites to honor fallen pilots. The term also encompasses individuals such as the girl being searched for within the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a9abe8221b156371ccb92c8c70ff3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5652d718e4ea5e4dc648511456987b2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8688e06b168deefda3fe220f725865&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9742ce4eb1971ba77904fc0e1868746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1172e16aec5fcaed74cebbab925fca42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc2240f2b9c03c7ee20a149da420ca0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c2bf1856c9246afe262f7402bdbfdc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1778833881</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
