    <node id="青雀">
      <data key="d0">青雀</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">青雀 (Qingque) is a character associated with the Xianzhou Luofu, specifically a member of the Divination Commission (太卜司). Known affectionately as a "sparrow," she is characterized by her love for playing the card game "帝垣琼玉牌" and her talent for skillfully balancing her work with moments of leisure, often managing to "slack off" while still completing her duties. She was assigned by the Diviner to wait at a card hall for distinguished guests and has successfully completed tasks such as activating three array bases and helping to restart the Qionguan Array. In her role, she helps guide visitors, is very familiar with the premises of the Divination Commission, and explains concepts like the Jade Abacus. She has also managed a library and has knowledge of the Jade Abacus (玉兆) technology. Her duties include operating the Zeus Combine Formation and discussing its functions with others, as well as reassuring companions about the nature of a Golden Human. She is knowledgeable about local lore, particularly concerning the "建木" (Jianmu), which she witnessed growing, and she has shown others the withered tree. After missions, she invites the Nameless to find her in "长乐天" (Changletian) for a game of cards and is also known to provide hints to unlock side doors.&lt;SEP&gt;青雀is a character from the Taibu Department who is known for being laid-back and familiar with shortcuts in the department.&lt;SEP&gt;青雀is a worker in the Divination Commission known for her relaxed attitude.&lt;SEP&gt;青雀is a character who frequents the Golden Man Lane in the Longle Sky, enjoys eating Chen Po's Tofu there, and often plays cards and slacks off.&lt;SEP&gt;青雀is a friend on the仙舟that三月七considers saying goodbye to.&lt;SEP&gt;青雀是小麻雀，提议教开拓者打帝垣琼玉牌，以便旅行时凑桌。&lt;SEP&gt;青雀(小麻雀)是仙舟罗浮的居民，热爱打帝垣琼玉牌，主动提出教开拓者和杨先生打牌，表示随时欢迎回来学习。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a9abe8221b156371ccb92c8c70ff3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7a23ca2f49ce8c9eb126529ef028cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d79ed550ca1869c633e5ee3153e644d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f8fa3030c9f0e45dc58488cd8c0b0b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2940364ce77c89b6b787e5861475970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aa978acb883a7010e681ac9415be70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b761f7975a148b7f60b9118ff40d2789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7f59f879256f855b57fd2b90f2f093&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3e68e248a108ebdbad18c906c7b760a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5341e4ccc7283969ac76c86061d28586&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b15f3e72ede1984381b5ab689b537e72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8b5bd13b0c402afd43298bddf26cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d71f2f56e13337663cff785e79fbb43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db1a6716eb95924fce53acec168f822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38d7d8ba8bfe5e69f41225515582546c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e5724440b453f77f33b2b72b886fc77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e44ecf966c6560c7f086afff655868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64341e8c7e20847211eae6769982882f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e021fc26775ae86ae4a8fa4b4a74a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee709ee6223dbebd15d8b80e4cdae7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6812b272464cfa07676db3909d99535</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1778835319</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="罗刹">
      <data key="d0">罗刹</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">罗刹 (Luocha) is a male character who primarily appears as a traveling merchant from beyond the Xianzhou (an "化外民"). He is known for transporting a mysterious coffin back to the Xianzhou and claims to draw power from the Aeon of Abundance (Yaoshi) while paradoxically opposing the Aeon himself. Throughout his journey, he demonstrates knowledge about Aeons and their histories, interacts with the Cloud Knights, and joins the protagonist (Trailblazer) in combat, often showing keen awareness of others' emotions. He is also a companion of 素裳, presenting himself as having medical expertise, which he successfully proves by repairing injuries on a mechanical judge. 罗刹 has visited the Star-Drifting Sea, where he consulted a diviner about his path, and has conversed with Dan Heng, suggesting they leave for now while mentioning that he has unfinished business.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a9abe8221b156371ccb92c8c70ff3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-488e16522a18a4f6bb0a292766e58c72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8688e06b168deefda3fe220f725865&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b031b1b4ab5aae362aa1180ca1fab1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39ee06bafb842d307b13ed54ad7ab232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56f9050ddaba5533f393398440a8cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86afcf1d5b41644aabd32c7cbee164cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-024d2e72f6f7b12c92caa76b22df8be2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1778833983</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="素裳">
      <data key="d0">素裳</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">素裳 (Sushang) is a young woman and a member of the Cloud Knights (云骑军) from the Xianzhou "Yaoqing" (仙舟「曜青」). In this role, she protects citizens and assists during incidents. She is characterized by her curiosity about various topics, including Aeons and their fates. Although trained in swordsmanship by her mother, she has limited formal education. As a Cloud Knight, she encounters a wounded mechanical judge and requests assistance from her companions, and she guides others to safe locations, expressing familiarity with the Alchemy Commission (丹鼎司). She also protects and helps the Trailblazer, promising to send them home after the battle, and notices when someone is injured, asking Dan Heng a simple question about his situation.&lt;SEP&gt;素裳是云骑军成员，调来罗浮仙舟后喜欢听书，向往成为大英雄，热爱云上五骁的故事，并提议下次带丹恒一起喝茶聊天。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a9abe8221b156371ccb92c8c70ff3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-488e16522a18a4f6bb0a292766e58c72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bf1da125b522014150884094e9e66e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8688e06b168deefda3fe220f725865&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b031b1b4ab5aae362aa1180ca1fab1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39ee06bafb842d307b13ed54ad7ab232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56f9050ddaba5533f393398440a8cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86afcf1d5b41644aabd32c7cbee164cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6812b272464cfa07676db3909d99535</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1778835322</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
