    <node id="梦">
      <data key="d0">梦</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">梦 (Dream) is a multifaceted concept and thematic element central to the narrative. It frequently refers to the dreamscape or dream state which serves as the primary setting for unfolding events, as indicated by various characters. 黄泉 mentions it as a place where she may have seen the 开拓者's figure, while 舒翁's statements confirm that character interactions occur within this dream. 流萤 defines 梦 as the essence of 星期七乐园, arguing that entering the乐园 equates to abandoning reality and immersing oneself in the dream. 拉格沃克•夏尔•米哈伊尔 recalls a long dream he had about the day he met 钟表小子, planning to record it at 流梦礁. 知更鸟 and 星期日 discuss the nature of 梦, with 知更鸟 attempting to awaken 星期日 from it. Furthermore, 梦 is identified as the dream state meticulously crafted by the "Order," from which characters are striving to awaken, representing a thematic concept of a reality from which people fear waking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50324d9549c90d9f6834f20f38e5f8a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f224a52938afe06f7dc4abae08d7f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded800b8093baab52c47d17c86d04375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e02a2272395c7c81c9cd1263f09605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6762f27a4d20dfd610a1155d60e87b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c86e4e8873e665dc85fecd7c393c16c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05a5c4612ea2ec33740c626cf9067e70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-950f3c9663f4eaa9cf5cef2539e2ff52</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779101382</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
