    <node id="梦泡">
      <data key="d0">梦泡</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dream bubbles (梦泡) are a concept and product within the world of Penacony. They are tangible carriers composed of "忆质" (Memory Mass) that store and allow users to experience the contents of dreams. Sold as memory-based items at venues like the Dreamscape Boutique by Edward the Physician, dream bubbles enable customers to relive the memories of others, including those of deceased figures such as Akivili. Each dream bubble is considered fun and uniquely tied to personal experiences. The concept is also used metaphorically, as Sampo compares the current state of Penacony to a dream bubble, and Firefly speculates that a strange dream location might be explained as one.&lt;SEP&gt;梦泡是忆质凝结成的物体，可以被忆者堆叠造成软着陆效果。&lt;SEP&gt;梦泡是匹诺康尼梦境中的体验内容，宾客可以随心所欲地体验，但无法带回现实。&lt;SEP&gt;梦泡is an artifact or concept left by the Watchmaker, a dream bubble containing a legacy.&lt;SEP&gt;梦泡refers to a dream bubble or memory bubble that contains the scenes from Misha's childhood.&lt;SEP&gt;梦泡(Dream Bubble) is a type of dream constructed from condensed memories, and the one in question appears empty but should not be able to form without content.&lt;SEP&gt;梦泡是米沙诞生的摇篮，也是他的家。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff01e303ac33cbdc731672f2b8068156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00d0fbb77db3436bd966280bc71989ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10a9a57ca0c7078de0765d59816cccd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39191a57b86d0c36329b9779dc5a8995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24bad56f5285fbbd948b8af133255ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f417d6e4dfdd365b59a413fbb957fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a141c2b9560a3be645dd178f945e028&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b85937e6bc111bb0516718814af5cb90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ccc378859a917598c9851df3b46abc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-399e9f5b95e2162b7f5074dcec92103a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76f30cea7751c5e1cdb8b78f14fea91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e64c4e33d4c17b896fbd12e80f65658f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74d9be5bb22932287cf5a631b7386195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b2df6c7c464d907afd4da6f5f01960</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779069358</data>
