    <node id="死亡">
      <data key="d0">死亡</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Death, within the context of Penacony, is a multifaceted entity, phenomenon, and concept. It is first investigated by Black Swan as a wandering threat within the dream, later identified as a nightmare entity or Memory Zone Meme that has indiscriminately attacked people, inducing mental or actual death. Initially concealed by the Family, who had promised absolute safety in the dream, the phenomenon became an urban legend that the Family attempts to suppress. Death is a central theme and key clue in several conspiracy theories, being strongly suspected as the murderer of Robin (知更鸟), evidenced by a distinctive wing-blade wound, an event allegedly covered up.

Death is a crucial element in various individuals' plans. For Saphing (砂金), it serves as both a bargaining chip and a target; he seeks to create a "most spectacular death" during his confrontation with Sunday (星期日) and dares to experiment with it within the dream, only on himself, to expose what he sees as the Family's only potential weakness and to cross into other dream layers. The concept is also discussed as a legendary event, with the Hunt family acknowledging that accidental deaths can occur even in a beautiful dream. It is linked to encounters with Firefly and the "Watchmaker" case, serving as vital evidence.

Furthermore, "Death" is the name given to the exile location of Dreamflux Reef, used by the Family to cover up their secrets. While the Family believes it to be a dangerous nightmare, local dreamscape residents consider it harmless. Ultimately, Death in Penacony represents a breach of promised safety, a mysterious killer, a method to bypass dream barriers, and a pivotal point around which many characters' schemes and the central conspiracy revolve.&lt;SEP&gt;死亡(Death) is an event that previously encountered米沙and流萤, later renamed to "沉睡" (Slumber).&lt;SEP&gt;死亡is a concept, referring to a "death" that has another side.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-24565d6d66fd343d204ca6ee232d3fb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b1268c29f322dda94efbb954a2bab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-083647d174927add1aefc63655ec615b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4006787ff76d5227d6ce51fce241de65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff5381ef14c0174d6621bf098b92d840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05a014c948b270f74369d5227c7fc80c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9de4b10f842bc7af36c30316a0a72a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c99e6308cd56f22b4ce44dda6f0ec62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f273e249d48375fe4ce18df04b167906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4f76837602b150702d42db6ea60525&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c0a3dbfcfd8b95ff234089961fba702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d69e5d473598eccb1e77a81726c583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dceb88ab2e44d48a689d3dca587728e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-319ffb461ba5f8c9e0f44cd7237080b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98bd728493101041950cb3bbec840969&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14ef88ed231842823bf1bb0651d40e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ef576bac7adaec894b503280717b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fc27eb1f7547ffdcf4c47fa1e6ca44c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23d4778f839d2a1eac66e3c79c7e10e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-591f11cf1ef3be84f3f140ad6ced600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c93d548b2a01ac78c4534185b1c50d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-745ef3f5cddfa7a86e439825e5de4a96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f9568f3044cc0b8024fbb468793c90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74d9be5bb22932287cf5a631b7386195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cca95c43061171ec0f9a64327c928c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05a52baa9f6e0386aac3ddefb6f99df9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-620e245cd9df09d58b2231e7fff3bf19</data>
