    <edge source="开拓者" target="星核">
      <data key="d7">26.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Trailblazer (开拓者) is defined by the presence of a Stellaron (星核) that has been implanted within their body in a stable state. This Stellaron is the same type of mysterious and dangerous substance that endangers worlds such as Jarilo-VI, making the Trailblazer a potential danger to others and a key concern for the crew of the Astral Express. The Stellaron is a core element of the Trailblazer's identity and destiny, granting them the ability to walk the Path of the Trailblaze and be glanced at by Nanook (纳努克), the Aeon of Destruction, which makes them more easily acknowledged by Aeons. The Trailblazer can hear the Stellaron's voice and resonate with it due to the Stellaron within them. A central task for the Trailblazer and their group is to locate and deal with the Stellaron in order to destroy it and end the disasters it causes; after the battle on Jarilo-VI, the Trailblazer has lingering questions about it. Walter (瓦尔特) confirmed that the Stellaron is connected to the crew's investigations, and the Trailblazer, who seeks to remove the Stellaron, mentioned in a dialogue that a "seed" is more powerful than the "Stellaron."&lt;SEP&gt;The Trailblazer asks why the Poor Observation Array cannot be used to calculate the location of the Stellaron.&lt;SEP&gt;开拓者asks how the Stellaron will be handled and offers help.&lt;SEP&gt;开拓者is familiar with the Stellaron and discusses its potential manipulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Trailblazer is identified as the bearer of a Stellaron.</data>
      <data key="d9">affliction,assistance,battle,bearing,celestial object,conflict,connection,contained within,containment,contains,destiny,destruction,goal,harboring,host,identity,inquiry,investigation,knowledge,location,mystery,possession,pursuit,questioning,resolution,search,stability,threat,体内共存,共鸣关系,寄宿关系,对话提及,寻找目标,持有,核心事件,比较,特殊性,载体包含</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-4dbaabda37c8db9a4a137cc6aa064f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8272ce558ae20153faafd6ffc5a4135d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3aa925e2cda548b4c1ed572e6b6fb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c61378b1f48a3fccbe0fff17273a16f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cbf01ed9ad87a70a79c843ac877485f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b90e0ee8e6c1bdf39a40aa9e79108543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a4d47602d8436e5950b7c64fa6734&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010cf81a86ef8e6d81978812db1537ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00732d55bdd6fa143033b2dd0669aaa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3da0cb92646701693c5ed26d30314d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb530c0e05d34c67f0c09a0b64e8fa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575eb06637f7ecf24d773fb6f0f798b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f1d50dd0c4a864aad264fdad2c99753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1381bbbb71b642a091a6c3425722884b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62249a61ab686e12d9f450bd5b82c692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-876cbdcb2b6b60cef20d49340ecee30f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7761bbe49cdee3fe2ebc6f41bfed7bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eacd315ae5f95c55d189019b4d765b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f371fb32e3b3a665db31402cdb619141&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63dc2a8cef74048f287c7e0648930116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d49ee9d93d2b9c97270455c78b3b83e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6bc51c0b8f913f809328ba29170426&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38d7d8ba8bfe5e69f41225515582546c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-024d2e72f6f7b12c92caa76b22df8be2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76f30cea7751c5e1cdb8b78f14fea91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafccb4855b4210dcf8ae59537a1eb77</data>
