    <edge source="开拓者" target="姬子">
      <data key="d7">46.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Himeko and the Trailblazer share a multi-faceted relationship encompassing mentorship, companionship, trust, and mutual respect. As the navigator of the Astral Express, Himeko first introduces herself to the Trailblazer after they awaken on the space station, showing concern and inviting them to join the train. She advises the Trailblazer to discover their own identity and learn to control the Stellaron through experience, encouraging them to master their own destiny. Himeko holds the Trailblazer in high regard, insisting they are essential to resolving critical situations.

As a companion, Himeko explains the nature and history of the Astral Express, and praises the Trailblazer’s contributions, assigning them tasks such as helping restart the train and leading a team to retrieve the Stellaron on Jarilo-VI. She provides critical intelligence and support via communication during missions, warns the Trailblazer about Kafka, and involves them in crew votes. The Trailblazer, in turn, worries about Himeko's situation. Himeko also instructs the Trailblazer to communicate answers to Sunday, and encourages them to find answers from personal experiences when facing challenges. In specific missions, Himeko proposes to investigate a murder case the Trailblazer witnessed, suggests they message Welt for updates, and recommends using the Clock trick again to resolve an interruption caused by Emily. Overall, the Trailblazer is a companion of Himeko aboard the Astral Express, and their dynamic is one of guidance, support, and light-hearted exchanges.&lt;SEP&gt;Himeko asks the Trailblazer if they remember finding a mysterious fragment when they entered the area.&lt;SEP&gt;姬子根据开拓者和三月七的投票结果，宣布团队的决定。&lt;SEP&gt;The Trailblazer proposes leaving with Himeko, and she agrees.</data>
