    <edge source="三月七" target="瓦尔特">
      <data key="d7">17.0</data>
      <data key="d8">三月七 and Welt Yang (often addressed by March 7th as "Uncle" or "Yang Shu") are companions who journey together as members of the same group, primarily within the context of the Astral Express crew. Their relationship is characterized by a clear mentor-student dynamic: March 7th frequently relies on Welt for guidance, following his instructions—such as using Six-Phase Ice to treat a wounded soldier—and seeking his advice on their next actions and decisions. Welt, in turn, provides practical direction and counsel, advising March 7th to slow down during a chase, telling her to stop joking and proceed forward, and comforting her by explaining that Fu Xuan is reasonable; he also proposes exploring Starhaven while waiting. He further shares his deductions about the mastermind behind the dream anomalies and the invitation's background. Welt also warns March 7th to be cautious during battles and encourages her and the Trailblazer to finish their tasks and return to the train soon. March 7th comments that Welt's deep thoughts can be overly sentimental, and she compares the Trailblazer's tendency to worry to Welt's, calling it un-energetic. Additionally, she remarks on a healer's strange appearance, prompting Welt to explain the Vidyadhara race. March 7th has also noted that Welt and Himeko have already disembarked the train, and Welt later informs the Trailblazer that March 7th and Himeko have departed for Flowdream Reef ahead of them.&lt;SEP&gt;三月七担忧瓦尔特的安危，对星期日的行为感到不满。&lt;SEP&gt;三月七affectionately calls瓦尔特 "Yang叔," showing their close bond as members of the Astral Express.</data>
      <data key="d9">address,advice,alert,alliance,caution,companion,comparison,concern,conversation,cooperation,coordination,crew member,critique,departure,explanation,friendship,inquiry,interaction,mediation,observation,protection,reference,response,shared objective,team member,teamwork,travel,先行,同行</data>
