    <edge source="丹恒" target="裂界">
      <data key="d7">8.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Dan Heng (丹恒) possesses significant knowledge about the Fragmentum and its creatures, understanding the nature of this erosion phenomenon on Jarilo-VI. He knows that objects created by the Fragmentum are forgeries, regardless of how real they appear, and that these residual images are unstable energy remnants. Dan Heng has been actively analyzing the Fragmentum’s pollution level as a means to gauge proximity to the Stellaron, and he has also noted that the fissure has a special connection with Cocolia, repeatedly recreating her image. While the Fragmentum has not yet eroded the immediate area, it has spawned monsters there, leading Dan Heng to comment that if the pollution continues unchecked, nearby shops and inns will face closure. Additionally, he has been trying to find an exit from the Fragmentum itself.</data>
      <data key="d9">analysis of pollution,connection,danger assessment,environment,escape,judgment,knowledge,location,observation,threat assessment,影响,评论</data>
