    <edge source="姬子" target="瓦尔特">
      <data key="d7">16.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Himeko and Welt Yang are fellow crew members traveling together on the Astral Express, established as colleagues after Welt was rescued by Himeko and Pom-Pom before beginning his journey with them. As part of their duties, they conduct observations and summarize results for the crew, and they have nearly exhausted topics of conversation with each other. They share a deep history, as Himeko has mentioned Welt’s old friend, indicating a past connection. In their interactions, Himeko comforts Welt by expressing trust that the Trailblazer will complete their mission, while Welt notes that he and Himeko will together face anyone who dares to provoke the train. He also contrasts their approaches to trusting a younger team, believing Himeko to be calmer and more willing to let go.

On specific missions, Himeko entrusts Welt with the task of remaining in reality and handling the Family, as she believes relying solely on him for negotiations with the Family is insufficient. They frequently discuss and analyze proposals, such as Black Swan's suggestions and anomalies in the dreamscape, and make plans to reunite and coordinate task assignments, including decisions to split into two groups. For example, Himeko and March 7th have already departed for Dreamflux Reef, with Welt informing the Trailblazer of their progress. Overall, their relationship is one of mutual trust and collaboration, marked by shared responsibilities and complementary perspectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Himeko tells Welt to return to the Astral Express with the Trailblazer while she handles hotel matters.</data>
      <data key="d9">alliance,camaraderie,collaboration,communication,coordination,crew communication,crew members,delegation,direction,discussion,insufficiency,meeting,observation,past,reliance,request,rescue,shared anger,shared knowledge,team coordination,team member,travel,信任,信任对比,先行,同伴关系,同行,团队合作,安慰</data>
