    <edge source="姬子" target="星期日">
      <data key="d7">8.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relationship between Himeko and Sunday is characterized by a series of profound philosophical debates and negotiations, primarily concerning the fate of others, the nature of freedom, and the ideals of Order. Himeko often challenges Sunday's discussions and statements. She directly demands clarity from him on the fate of Mr. Yang and Robin, and she personally questions Sunday's concept of a "paradise" built upon Order, arguing that it is merely another form of imprisonment and manipulation. Himeko analyzes that Sunday is deeply convinced of his ideals for Order and genuinely wants to prove them correct. She believes that Sunday's narrative, as seen through the story of the dream-chasers, allowed him to profoundly recognize the limitations of "using strength to aid the weak." Furthermore, Himeko points out that Sunday's arguments tend to focus more on the spiritual plight of people rather than their physical imprisonment. Despite her critiques, at other times, Himeko remains silent in response to Sunday's discourses. Ultimately, Sunday engages in a discussion with Himeko about the Aeons and formally extends an invitation to her, indicating a complex dynamic of ideological confrontation and attempted persuasion between them.</data>
      <data key="d9">analysis,belief,challenge,conflict,confrontation,dialogue,insight,invitation,negotiation,observation,沉默,理念冲突,观察,解读,评论,质疑</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-2ab104d64e9eb410cea34464f76c33a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d81d7afd4e410e297a5351eee7eb9d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6762f27a4d20dfd610a1155d60e87b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded3035b9d576152c6b6ec854c5ffeed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3889b67baa0c9d0549e50a6f4357f9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cca95c43061171ec0f9a64327c928c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9189bbff0cdab4202d189f24260b142b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-634037196a7f2b333524f9f78739583e</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
