    <edge source="匹诺康尼" target="流萤">
      <data key="d7">20.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Fleur's relationship with Penacony is multifaceted. She is known as a visitor, a Stowaway, and an interstellar refugee who was accepted by the Family within the city. In Penacony, Fleur often acts as a guide for the Trailblazer, enthusiastically sharing her love for the city and introducing its famous locations and characters. She considers Penacony a “dreamland” and a paradise that can accept her, and she is willing to treat the Trailblazer to the city’s representative cuisine. As a Stowaway, her presence in the Dreamscape is initially clandestine, and she is said to have completely vanished from both dreams and reality after a certain incident. She is intimately familiar with the dreamscape of Penacony, often comparing strange new dreams with the more familiar ones she knows. In certain narratives, such as in films, Fleur's performances are set within the context of Penacony, where she displays excitement and thrill for her stimulating life in the city.&lt;SEP&gt;流萤在心灰意冷时考虑离开匹诺康尼。&lt;SEP&gt;流萤decides to accompany the星穹列车through the rest of their journey in匹诺康尼.&lt;SEP&gt;流萤observes that匹诺康尼is full of talented people and suggests heading towards their destination there.&lt;SEP&gt;Firefly comments on the Trailblazer's reactions to stimuli in Penacony.&lt;SEP&gt;流萤's journey is to Penacony, the dreamland, where she must experience three 'deaths'.</data>
